You know, my son is right in that age range where we've got Harry Potter over here.
你知道，我儿子正处于那个年龄段，我们这边到处都是哈利·波特。

447
00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:52.460
And we reached out to Jen about this.
我们为此联系了简。

448
00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:52.900
Yeah.
是啊。

449
00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:55.000
What was up with the Harry Potter thing?
哈利·波特是怎么回事？

450
00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.060
Yeah, I was so curious.
是啊，我太好奇了。

451
00:23:56.240 --> 00:23:59.260
I was like, was this like an inside joke in the writer's room?
我当时就在想，这是编剧室里的内部梗吗？

452
00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:00.740
And this is what Jen had to say.
这是珍（Jen）的回答。

453
00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:05.160
We had a bunch of Harry Potter fans in the writer's room.
我们编剧室里有一群《哈利·波特》的粉丝。

454
00:24:05.320 --> 00:24:13.320
It even evolved to a situation where we had chopsticks hanging around the room from takeout,
后来情况甚至演变成，我们屋里到处都是吃外卖剩下的筷子，

455
00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:15.980
you know, because we ate a lot of our meals in the writer's room.
你知道的，因为我们很多顿饭都是在编剧室里吃的。

456
00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:23.200
And so one afternoon, we decorated our chopsticks while we were probably pitching stories and jokes.
所以有一天下午，我们一边构思故事和笑话，一边把筷子装饰了一下。

457
00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:24.900
We each decorated chopsticks.
我们每个人都装饰了自己的筷子。

458
00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:32.020
And then we had, we were pretending that they were Harry Potter wands and we would do spells on each other.
然后我们假装那是《哈利·波特》里的魔杖，还会互相施咒。

459
00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.360
Probably just comedy spells.
大概就是些搞笑的咒语吧。

460
00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:40.360
But we even had wand stands near the writer's room door that were just little thumbtacks,
我们甚至在编剧室门口装了魔杖架，其实就是几个图钉，

461
00:24:40.560 --> 00:24:43.020
you know, spread apart so that we would rest our wands on them.
你知道的，把它们分开钉好，这样我们就能把魔杖架在上面。

462
00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:49.140
So everybody had their Harry Potter chopstick wands and our wand stands.
所以每个人都有自己的《哈利·波特》筷子魔杖和魔杖架。

463
00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:51.980
And that sounds super dorky.
听起来超级书呆子气的。

464
00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:54.420
And I believe it is.
我也觉得是。

465
00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:55.520
It was really fun.
但真的很有趣。

466
00:24:56.620 --> 00:25:00.840
Once again, what the writers were doing to procrastinate made it into a script.
又一次，编剧们为了拖延工作而做的事情被写进了剧本里。

467
00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:05.000
Yeah, I feel like there's probably more of that than we will ever know.
是啊，我觉得这种情况可能比我们知道的还要多。

468
00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:06.720
Yes, exactly.
没错，确实如此。

469
00:25:07.340 --> 00:25:07.820
All right.
好吧。

470
00:25:07.960 --> 00:25:11.460
So at seven minutes, six seconds, Michael has his big survivor speech.
在七分零六秒的时候，迈克尔发表了他的大型《幸存者》演讲。

471
00:25:11.460 --> 00:25:17.880
Now, you guys, we've shared this before, but our camera operators, Randall and Matt, both
各位，我们之前分享过，我们的摄影师兰德尔（Randall）和马特（Matt）都

472
00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:19.400
