参与过《幸存者》的拍摄。

473
00:25:19.540 --> 00:25:23.680
So this had to have been a little bit of an interesting callback for them, right, Jenna?
所以这对他们来说一定是个有趣的致敬，对吧，珍娜（Jenna）？

474
00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:25.140
Well, yes.
嗯，是的。

475
00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:30.440
And how prepared were they to lug cameras on their shoulders on a beach?
他们对于扛着摄像机在沙滩上奔波准备得如何？

476
00:25:30.620 --> 00:25:34.780
I mean, these guys, they were like, oh, I've come full circle.
我是说，他们当时就像是，噢，我这算是圆满了。

477
00:25:34.980 --> 00:25:35.740
Yeah, bring it.
没错，来吧。

478
00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:41.640
So Michael says this, a group of Americans will undergo the ultimate challenge.
迈克尔是这么说的：一群美国人将接受终极挑战。

479
00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:48.380
One day, 14 strangers who work together, but only one survivor.
有一天，14个在一起工作的陌生人，但只有一个幸存者。

480
00:25:48.620 --> 00:25:49.700
And they're all like, what?
而他们全都一脸懵：什么？

481
00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:52.040
What's about to happen here?
这到底要发生什么？

482
00:25:53.180 --> 00:25:56.880
Well, what's about to happen is a spoon and egg race, Angela.
嗯，接下来要发生的是勺子运蛋比赛，安吉拉（Angela）。

483
00:25:57.400 --> 00:25:58.240
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

484
00:25:59.360 --> 00:26:02.920
Except the person with the egg will be blindfolded.
只不过拿蛋的人要被蒙上眼睛。

485
00:26:03.040 --> 00:26:08.640
Also, Jenna, I don't know if you remember this, but poor Brian, they had him in the background.
还有，珍娜，不知道你还记不记得，可怜的布莱恩（Brian），他们让他待在背景里。

486
00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:10.500
He's just eating his egg.
他就在那儿吃他的蛋。

487
00:26:11.680 --> 00:26:14.420
He's eating, and it didn't make it on camera.
他在吃，但没被拍进镜头里。

488
00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:19.540
And I remember feeling so bad that Brian, in the course of this time, in the heat, had
我记得当时觉得布莱恩太惨了，在那段时间里，在那种高温下，

489
00:26:19.540 --> 00:26:21.900
to eat hard-boiled eggs and hot dogs.
还得吃水煮蛋和热狗。

490
00:26:21.920 --> 00:26:23.120
I was like, this poor guy.
我当时心想，这可怜的家伙。

491
00:26:23.340 --> 00:26:27.260
And also, I think it's very funny that Michael hard-boiled the eggs.
而且我觉得迈克尔把蛋煮熟了这一点非常搞笑。

492
00:26:28.400 --> 00:26:28.900
Yes!
没错！

493
00:26:29.360 --> 00:26:32.460
Because then if they fall off the spoon, it doesn't matter.
因为这样就算蛋从勺子上掉下来也没关系。

494
00:26:32.780 --> 00:26:33.400
There's no point.
根本没意义。

495
00:26:33.620 --> 00:26:34.400
There's no point.
确实没意义。

496
00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:40.880
Now, I am wondering, and I don't know the answer, I am speculating, but I wonder if we
现在我在想，我不知道答案，我只是在猜测，我在想我们是不是

497
00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:48.500
had to hard-boil the eggs because we couldn't risk having eggs break on the beach and sort
必须把蛋煮熟，因为我们不能冒着蛋在沙滩上摔碎的风险，

498
00:26:48.500 --> 00:26:50.780
of leaving behind that kind of debris.
那样会留下那种残渣。

499
00:26:50.780 --> 00:26:54.920
Because when we left there, we had to make it seem like we'd never been there at all.
因为当我们离开那里时，我们必须让现场看起来就像我们从没来过一样。

500
00:26:55.040 --> 00:27:00.860
Not only that, but there's no way we could be dealing with wardrobe issues with egg yolk.
不仅如此，我们可没法处理蛋黄弄脏戏服的问题。

501
00:27:01.260 --> 00:27:02.660
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

502
00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:08.940
But I like to think that it was just Michael's strange choice, but it was probably a very,
但我愿意相信这只是迈克尔奇怪的选择，不过这可能是一个非常、

503
00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:10.060
very practical one.
非常务实的选择。

504
00:27:10.180 --> 00:27:11.420
Oh, I'm sure it was very thought out.
哦，我敢肯定这是经过深思熟虑的。

505
00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:13.040
I wrote, what the heck?
我写道，这到底是什么鬼？

506
00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:15.260
Who is setting up these tiki torches?
是谁在布置这些火把？

507
00:27:15.420 --> 00:27:17.000
Where did the blindfolds come in?
眼罩是从哪儿来的？

508
00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:18.180
Who carried the eggs?
谁搬的鸡蛋？

509
00:27:18.280 --> 00:27:19.160
Who had the spoons?
谁拿的勺子？

510
00:27:19.360 --> 00:27:20.440
What is happening?
到底发生了什么？

511
00:27:21.620 --> 00:27:27.460
Oh, Angela, I don't know if it's in the deleted scenes, but in the script, there was an extra
哦，安吉拉，我不知道这是否在删减片段里，但在剧本中，有一个额外的

